# UI translations (all four apps)

Canonical: `docs/DEV.md` § Languages. Vision §23.

## Rule

- English source = `en()` in that app’s `src/locale.rs` only.
- Every other catalogue language = `translations/<code>.tsv` (one `key<TAB>text` per `en` key, `{placeholders}` kept).
- **Never** add a user-visible label only in English. After editing `en()`, update **all** packs for that app.
- No shared i18n crate — duplicate the workflow per app (copy-then-diverge).

## When you add or change a string

```bash
# after editing apps/<app>/src/locale.rs en()
./scripts/scaffold-ui-translations.sh --app <app> --standin-english
# replace English stand-ins in apps/<app>/translations/*.tsv (agent / manual)
./scripts/check-ui-translations.sh --app <app>
```

Or edit the new TSV rows by hand, then run the check. Prefer bash (or a
Rust tool) — **no Python** for this workflow (see `no-python-scripts.mdc`).
`cargo test -p <crate> --lib every_catalogue_language_translates_every_key`
must stay green.

## Do not

- Reintroduce `locale_chrome.rs` or a “29 language” subset that leaves catalogue entries in English.
- Ship with `KUMKAJ_ALLOW_TRANSLATION_GAPS=1` (fill-pipeline only).
- Copy TSV packs between apps — each app’s `en()` key set differs.
